# Qt's scene graph does not release its textures and pixmaps when a QQuickWindow
# is torn down inside a headless test process. The allocations are real but they
# are Qt's, not ours, and there is no API to force the render context to drop
# them. Suppressed by module so that leaks in our own code still fail the build.
leak:libQt6Quick.so
leak:libQt6QuickControls2.so
leak:libQt6Qml.so
leak:libQt6Gui.so

# QPdfDocument leaks its asynchronous loader's buffer when a load ends in an
# error -- reached through load(QString) as much as load(QIODevice*), so there is
# no overload to choose instead and nothing of ours to free. Suppressed by module
# like the rest: a leak in our own code still fails the build.
leak:libQt6Pdf.so

# libgit2 keeps its error text in per-thread state, allocated the first time a call
# on that thread fails -- which happens routinely, because discovery walking up from
# a folder that is in no work tree *is* a failed call. That state is freed when the
# thread exits or when git_libgit2_shutdown() runs on the same thread, and a task
# pool thread still alive at process exit satisfies neither. Nothing of ours to free
# and no API to force it: git_error_clear() drops the message and keeps the buffer.
# Suppressed by module like the rest.
leak:libgit2.so
